  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the tandoor to 450°F (230°C).",
    "Trim the lamb shoulder of excess fat and cut it into 1-inch (2.5 cm) pieces.",
    "In a large bowl, combine the lamb, sun-dried tomatoes, onion, garlic, cumin, coriander, paprika, salt, and black pepper. Mix well to coat the lamb evenly.",
    "Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the lamb mixture to the skillet and cook, stirring occasionally, until the lamb is browned on all sides, about 5 minutes.",
    "Transfer the lamb mixture to the preheated tandoor and cook for 30 minutes.",
    "Meanwhile, chop the fresh parsley and set aside.",
    "After 30 minutes, remove the lamb from the tandoor and stir in the lemon juice.",
    "Serve the lamb hot in a korean-brass-bowl, garnished with chopped parsley.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!"
  ],
